From 13d0a50fb4f35434074e8daabb1e03be5e64d92d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sm64ds-3ds <244728604+ethanseagull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 05:27:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] hal: the hosted particle callback tables carry the
 Itanium head on the 3DS

On the 3DS the tracker's constructor is GCC C++, and GCC's constructors
install `table + 8`, the address point past [offset-to-top][typeinfo]. For
the eight callback classes whose key function only a host face defines, the
link keeps these hosted two-word arrays (linkfix HOST_KEEP), so slot 1 was
read from past their end: null, the first time a level's tracker updated a
water callback (Jolly Roger Bay, once Stage::Render ran). Under
SM64DS_HOST_3DS every table gets the two head words (VT_HEAD) and the
startup check reads past them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 port/hal/particle_vtable.cpp | 68 ++++++++++++++++++++++--------------
 1 file changed, 41 insertions(+), 27 deletions(-)

diff --git a/port/hal/particle_vtable.cpp b/port/hal/particle_vtable.cpp
index 75f4866ef..e0e675b13 100644
--- a/port/hal/particle_vtable.cpp
+++ b/port/hal/particle_vtable.cpp
@@ -105,78 +105,92 @@ void _ZN5dPa_c7level_c23cleanParticleCallback_c8OnUpdateERN8Particle6SystemEb(vo
 #define SPAWN(f) ((void *)&f)
 #define UPDATE(f) ((void *)&f)
 
+/* THE 3DS STORES THE ADDRESS POINT. The tracker's constructor is real C++ on
+   the 3DS (GCC), and GCC's constructors install `table + 8`, the Itanium
+   address point past [offset-to-top][typeinfo]. Where one of these arrays is
+   the table the link keeps (port3ds/tools/linkfix.py's HOST_KEEP: the eight
+   whose key function only a host face defines), it must carry those two words
+   in front, or slot 1 is read from past its end. VT_HEAD is them. */
+#if defined(SM64DS_HOST_3DS)
+#define VT_HEAD 2
+#define VT_HEAD_WORDS 0, 0,
+#else
+#define VT_HEAD 0
+#define VT_HEAD_WORDS
+#endif
+
